=====================================================================
SUMMARY
=====================================================================

  * No GPL, LGPL, AGPL or MPL license appears among the dependencies of any
    published artifact, nor among the development dependencies. The only
    copyleft license in the project is Núcleo's own AGPL-3.0-or-later.
  * The `nucleo` binary links the Go standard library and 14 third-party Go
    modules, all BSD-3-Clause or MIT, plus SQLite, which is in the public domain.
    Two of the modules are linked only on macOS and Windows, and one only on
    Linux and macOS (table below).
  * The npm package @nucleoledger/verify has ZERO runtime dependencies: it
    contains only Núcleo's own code.
  * The static verifier page (web/verify) and the PHP SDK (sdk/php) contain only
    Núcleo's own code.

=====================================================================
1. WHAT TRAVELS IN EACH PUBLISHED ARTIFACT
=====================================================================

1.1  The `nucleo` binary (GitHub release archives)
---------------------------------------------------

Built with CGO_ENABLED=0 for six platforms: linux, darwin and windows, each for
amd64 and arm64. Modules linked, per `go list -deps` for each platform:

| module | version | license | platforms where it is linked |
|---|---|---|---|
| Go standard library and runtime | go1.27.1 at release time | BSD-3-Clause | the six |
| github.com/dustin/go-humanize | v1.0.1 | MIT | the six |
| github.com/google/uuid | v1.6.0 | BSD-3-Clause | linux/amd64, linux/arm64, darwin/amd64, darwin/arm64 |
| github.com/mattn/go-isatty | v0.0.24 | MIT | darwin/amd64, darwin/arm64, windows/amd64, windows/arm64 |
| github.com/ncruces/go-strftime | v1.0.0 | MIT | darwin/amd64, darwin/arm64, windows/amd64, windows/arm64 |
| github.com/remyoudompheng/bigfft | v0.0.0-20230129092748-24d4a6f8daec | BSD-3-Clause | the six |
| github.com/shurlinet/go-slip39 | v0.1.0 | MIT | the six |
| golang.org/x/crypto | v0.56.0 | BSD-3-Clause | the six |
| golang.org/x/mod | v0.40.0 | BSD-3-Clause | the six |
| golang.org/x/sys | v0.47.0 | BSD-3-Clause | the six |
| golang.org/x/term | v0.45.0 | BSD-3-Clause | the six |
| modernc.org/libc | v1.75.6 | BSD-3-Clause (+ its third-party notices: Go, BSD-3-Clause; musl, MIT) | the six |
| modernc.org/mathutil | v1.7.1 | BSD-3-Clause | the six |
| modernc.org/memory | v1.12.1 | BSD-3-Clause (+ code from Go and mmap-go, both BSD-3-Clause) | the six |
| modernc.org/sqlite | v1.58.0 | BSD-3-Clause (+ SQLite, public domain) | the six |

Present in go.mod or go.sum but NOT linked into the binary on any of the six
platforms: the rest of the module graph (build tooling of modernc.org, such as
modernc.org/ccgo, and golang.org/x/net, x/sync, x/text, x/tools and others).
Inside modernc.org/sqlite, the sqlite-vec extension (MIT) is not compiled into
the binary on any platform, and the logo of modernc.org/memory is an image that
is not compiled either.

The release archives contain this NOTICE, next to LICENSE, AUTHORS, README.md,
CHANGELOG.md and three documents from docs/ (from the first release after
2026-09-26; v0.1.0-alpha and v0.2.0-alpha did not include it).

1.2  The npm package @nucleoledger/verify
------------------------------------------

`dependencies`, `peerDependencies`, `optionalDependencies` and
`bundleDependencies` are all empty. The published tarball contains dist/,
README.md, LICENSE and package.json: Núcleo's own code only.
License: AGPL-3.0-or-later.

1.3  The static verifier page (web/verify)
-------------------------------------------

nucleo-verify.js is built by esbuild from the sources of sdk/ts, which have no
runtime dependencies. It contains no third-party code and no third-party license
or copyright notice.

1.4  The PHP SDK (sdk/php)
--------------------------

No composer, no bundled third-party code. At runtime it needs PHP 8.0+ with the
sodium and json extensions, which the host provides; they are not distributed
with Núcleo.

1.5  The integration example (examples/erp-node)
------------------------------------------------

Depends only on @nucleoledger/verify (Núcleo itself, AGPL-3.0-or-later).

=====================================================================
2. DEVELOPMENT, TEST AND RELEASE ONLY — NOT DISTRIBUTED
=====================================================================

2.1  sdk/ts development dependencies
-------------------------------------

Direct: esbuild 0.25.0 (MIT), typescript 5.7.3 (Apache-2.0), vitest 5.0.1 (MIT).
The whole installed tree, read from package-lock.json and, where the lockfile
has no license field, from each installed package.json or from the npm registry:

    MIT            107 packages (includes the 25 platform binaries of esbuild)
    Apache-2.0       2 packages  typescript 5.7.3, expect-type 1.4.0
    ISC              2 packages  picocolors 1.1.1, siginfo 2.0.0
    BSD-3-Clause     1 package   source-map-js 1.2.1

None of them is copyleft, and none is in the published package.

2.2  Go: test-only modules
--------------------------

None. The Go tests, with and without the `testhooks` build tag, compile no
module that the binary does not already link.

2.3  Python oracles (testdata/vectors/*/generar.py, internal/store/testdata)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Python standard library only, except testdata/vectors/receipt/generar.py, which
uses the `cryptography` package (Apache-2.0 OR BSD-3-Clause) for Ed25519. It is
not pinned in the repository: it is the one the system provides (3.4.8 on the
machine where this inventory was taken).

2.4  Build, signing and release tooling
---------------------------------------

Go toolchain (BSD-3-Clause), GoReleaser (MIT), cosign (Apache-2.0), and the
GitHub Actions used by the workflows: actions/checkout, actions/setup-go,
actions/setup-node, actions/attest-build-provenance, goreleaser/goreleaser-action,
shivammathur/setup-php (MIT) and sigstore/cosign-installer (Apache-2.0). They
build and sign what is published; none of their code is inside it.

=====================================================================
3. THIRD-PARTY TEST DATA IN THE REPOSITORY
=====================================================================

Only in the source tree, in no published artifact:

  * testdata/vectors/slip39/vectors.json — the 45 official SLIP-0039 vectors,
    downloaded from Trezor's python-shamir-mnemonic repository, whose license
    GitHub reports as MIT. sha256 recorded in testdata/vectors/README.md.
  * testdata/vectors/jcs/rfc8785-3.2.3 — the example of RFC 8785 §3.2.3.
  * testdata/vectors/merkle/rfc6962 — the Merkle tree test data of Google's
    Certificate Transparency project, as found today in
    github.com/transparency-dev/merkle (testonly/constants.go and
    testonly/reference_test.go, commit fbbcd741), whose license is Apache-2.0,
    Copyright Google LLC. Where they were copied from when they were added
    (2026-09-04) was not recorded; on 2026-09-26 every value was compared with
    that repository and recomputed from RFC 9162 §2.1, and all of them match.
    Details and sha256 in testdata/vectors/README.md.
  * internal/keys/keys_test.go — the test vectors of RFC 8032 §7.1.

=====================================================================
4. HOW THIS INVENTORY WAS TAKEN
=====================================================================

    # modules linked into the binary, per release platform
    CGO_ENABLED=0 GOOS=<os> GOARCH=<arch> go list -deps \
        -f '{{with .Module}}{{.Path}}{{end}}' ./cmd/nucleo | sort -u
    # the same, from a built binary
    go version -m <binary>
    # modules compiled by the tests
    go list [-tags testhooks] -deps -test \
        -f '{{with .Module}}{{.Path}}{{end}}' ./...
    # license files: read from $(go env GOMODCACHE)/<module>@<version>/
    # npm: the `license` field of sdk/ts/package-lock.json, then of each
    #      installed package.json, then `npm view <package>@<version> license`

Every license was identified by reading its text, not by its file name.

